[{"text":"Overview.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"FeynCalc is equipped with special symbols that facilitate calculations involving light-cone vectors. The default n and \\bar{n} vectors are defined via the global variables $FCDefaultLightconeVectorN and $FCDefaultLightconeVectorNB. By default those are set to FCGV[\"n\"] and FCGV[\"nb\"] to avoid possible conflicts with user-defined variables","anchor":"notation-for-light-cone-components","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{$FCDefaultLightconeVectorN, $FCDefaultLightconeVectorNB}","anchor":"cb1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\{\\text{FCGV}(\\text{n}),\\text{FCGV}(\\text{nb})\\}","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"These names can be of course changed. A particularly convenient choice is to use n and nb. Notice that these commands must be evaluated at the beginning of every FeynCalc session","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"$FCDefaultLightconeVectorN = n; $FCDefaultLightconeVectorNB = nb;","anchor":"cb2","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"Apart from this you must also explicitly define the values of the scalar products \\(n^2\\), \\bar{n}^2 and \\(n \\cdot \\bar{n}\\)","anchor":"cb2-2","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"FCClearScalarProducts[] ScalarProduct[n] = 0; ScalarProduct[nb] = 0; ScalarProduct[n, nb] = 2;","anchor":"cb3","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"The Plus, Minus and peRpendicular components of 4-vectors are called FVLP, FVLN and FVLR respectively. The plus and minus components are immediately rewritten into forms involving \\(n\\) and \\bar{n}. The perpendicular component is a separate entity that cannot be simplified further.","anchor":"cb3-4","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{FVLP[p, \\[Mu]], FVLN[p, \\[Mu]], FVLR[p, \\[Mu]]}","anchor":"cb4","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} \\overline{\\text{nb}}^{\\mu } \\left(\\overline{n}\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right),\\frac{1}{2} \\overline{n}^{\\mu } \\left(\\overline{\\text{nb}}\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right),\\overline{p}^{\\mu }{}_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{FVLPD[p, \\[Mu]], FVLND[p, \\[Mu]], FVLRD[p, \\[Mu]]}","anchor":"cb5","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} \\;\\text{nb}^{\\mu } (n\\cdot p),\\frac{1}{2} n^{\\mu } (\\text{nb}\\cdot p),p^{\\mu }{}_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"It is also possible to specify your own symbols for the light-cone vectors thus overriding what is set via the global variables","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"FVLR[p, mu, myN, myNB] % // FCI // StandardForm","anchor":"cb6","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{mu}}{}_{\\perp }\\]","anchor":"cb6-2","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"(*Pair[LightConePerpendicularComponent[LorentzIndex[mu], Momentum[myN], Momentum[myNB]], LightConePerpendicularComponent[Momentum[p], Momentum[myN], Momentum[myNB]]]*)","anchor":"cb7","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"Internally, the perpendicular component is implemented as an extra head wrapped around such internal symbols as LorentzIndex or Momentum. This head is called LightConePerpendicularComponent and has 3 arguments. The last two arguments specify the light-cone vectors.","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"?LightConePerpendicularComponent","anchor":"cb8","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"The pattern introduced for 4-vectors can be also found when working scalar products, metric tensors or Dirac matrices","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{SPLP[p, q], SPLN[p, q], SPLR[p, q]}","anchor":"cb9","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\overline{n}\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right) \\left(\\overline{\\text{nb}}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right),\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\overline{n}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right) \\left(\\overline{\\text{nb}}\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right),\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{SPLPD[p, q], SPLND[p, q], SPLRD[p, q]}","anchor":"cb10","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} (n\\cdot p) (\\text{nb}\\cdot q),\\frac{1}{2} (n\\cdot q) (\\text{nb}\\cdot p),p\\cdot q_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb10-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{MTLP[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]], MTLN[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]], MTLR[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]]}","anchor":"cb11","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} \\overline{n}^{\\nu } \\overline{\\text{nb}}^{\\mu },\\frac{1}{2} \\overline{n}^{\\mu } \\overline{\\text{nb}}^{\\nu },\\bar{g}^{\\mu \\nu }{}_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb11-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{GALP[\\[Mu]], GALN[\\[Mu]], GALR[\\[Mu]]}","anchor":"cb12","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} \\overline{\\text{nb}}^{\\mu } \\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{n},\\frac{1}{2} \\overline{n}^{\\mu } \\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{\\text{nb}},\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }{}_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"{GSLP[\\[Mu]], GSLN[\\[Mu]], GSLR[\\[Mu]]}","anchor":"cb13","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"\\[\\left\\{\\frac{1}{2} \\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{n} \\left(\\overline{\\text{nb}}\\cdot \\overline{\\mu }\\right),\\frac{1}{2} \\left(\\overline{n}\\cdot \\overline{\\mu }\\right) \\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{\\text{nb}},\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{\\mu }_{\\perp }\\right\\}\\]","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"Contracting the full metric tensor with the perpendicular component returns the latter","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"Notation for light-cone components"},{"text":"MT[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]] MTLR[\\[Mu], \\[Rho]] % // Contract","anchor":"cb14","section":"Notation for light-cone components"}]